2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* v7fs.c, v7fs.h: fold the V6 and 2.11BSD backends into the V7 engine
	(v6fs.c and bsd211fs.c deleted).  V6's s_isize-as-block-count, 32-byte
	inode and ILARG bmap, and 2.11BSD's 4-byte block addresses and
	variable-length directory entries, become per-edition ops in the shared
	engine.
	* byteorder.c, byteorder.h: byte-order ops table (bo_le/bo_be/bo_me),
	the single copy of each little-/big-/middle-endian primitive.
	* filsys_format.c: per-edition descriptor table; filsys_getformat()
	returns filsys_edition_t, which carries both the descriptor and the
	runtime state.
	* filsys.c: route every operation through the descriptor's ops table
	(forty edition comparisons down to two).
	* Makefile.am: drop v6fs.[ch] and bsd211fs.[ch]; add byteorder.[ch]
	and filsys_format.c.

2026-09-05  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* filsys.c: edition_bsize() per-edition block size (the open path had
	a ternary that omitted 2.11BSD); truncate zero-fill buffer sized to
	V7_MAXBSIZE instead of 512 bytes.
	* test_matrix.c: name-length matrix at 14/30/63/64 for every edition.

2026-09-05  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* filsys.c: max_namlen() per-edition name limit; the facade's
	path-component buffer was 15 bytes for every edition, so 2.11BSD's
	63-character names were rejected before reaching the backend.
	* test_matrix.c: name-length regression (63 for bsd211, 14 for v7).

2026-09-05  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* bsd211fs.c, bsd211fs.h: new backend for 2.11BSD (4-byte block
	addresses, di_flags, symlinks, variable-length directory entries).
	* v7fs.c, v7fs.h: Xenix (mode 3) and 2.9BSD (mode 4) support; the block
	size is now a runtime property (512 or 1024); Xenix magic validation at
	superblock offset 1016.
	* mkfs.filsys.c: mkfs for Xenix, 2.9BSD and 2.11BSD; the v7fs mkfs path
	is generalized to 1024-byte blocks, per-edition byte order, free-cache
	width and address count.
	* mount.filsys.c, fsck.filsys.c, mkfs.filsys.c: require -v (no default
	edition); 32v renamed vax32.
	* filsys.h, filsys.c, filsys_ops.h, test_matrix.c: FILSYS_BSD211
	edition; test_matrix covers all nine editions.
	* filsys.5, mount.filsys.1, fsck.filsys.1, mkfs.filsys.1,
	findfs.filsys.1, README.md: document the new editions and the rename.

2026-08-31  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* mount.filsys.c, findfs.filsys.c: renamed from filsysmount.c and
	  filsysfind.c to match the `<verb>.filsys` binary names.
	* mkfs.filsys.c: new tool; create a V7 filesystem (superblock, i-list,
	  interleaved free list, root directory) in a disk image.  -o block
	  offset; -b boot block (a PDP-11 a.out, V7 magic 0407).
	* fsck.filsys.c: new tool; thin wrapper over v7fs_check().
	* mkfs.filsys.1, fsck.filsys.1, findfs.filsys.1, mount.filsys.1:
	  renamed man pages with .SH NAME lines so `man -k` finds them.
	* Makefile.am, configure.ac, .gitignore, packaging/, README.distributions,
	  COPYING, NEWS: updated for the new tool names and the two new tools.

